course: dictionary
lesson: 9762
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show which meaning the writer means. In «I'm a Liverpool supporter», the clue is the football team, so a supporter is a person who likes and cheers for a team.
explain: Now read «Some people blame energy prices, and each view has supporters.» Here there is no team. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Try your meaning in the sentence: each view has people who agree with it and help it. That is the second meaning of supporter.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: A supporter is a person who likes and cheers for a sports team.
fact: A supporter is also a person who agrees with and helps an idea, a person, or a cause.
fact: «Some people blame energy prices, and each view has supporters» means each view has people who agree with it.
fact: In the UK and Australia, «supporter» is the usual word for a football fan. In the US, people say «fan».
fact: Charities thank their supporters, because supporters give time or money to help.
exercise: «I'm a Liverpool supporter.» What does supporter mean? | A person who holds up a heavy bag | A person who writes news reports | *A person who cheers for a sports team | A person who runs very fast
exercise: «Each view has supporters.» What does supporter mean here? | People who count the money | People who blame energy prices | People who sell energy | *People who agree with that view
exercise: A charity thanks its supporters. Who are they? | People who read the news | People who run the shops in the street | *People who give time or money to help the charity | Animals that live near the charity
test: «Their supporters sang loudly as the team ran out.» Who are the supporters? | *People who cheer for the team | The players on the pitch | The people selling ice cream | The referees in black
test: «Many people are supporters of the new park plan.» What does supporters mean? | People who visit the park on Sundays | People who dig the ground | *People who agree with and help the plan | People who are against the plan
exam: Which meaning of supporter fits «The charity needs more supporters to give money each month»? | A person who runs a sports team | A person who has a bad cough | A person who holds something up | *A person who gives help to a cause
